      "content": "While some may suggest taking lower doses, the safest course of action is to consult your doctor before taking any medication with sertraline, even if it's just for short-term relief. Dosages of over-the-counter medications can vary, but it's crucial to follow the recommended dosage to avoid adverse effects. If you must get rest, try other methods to soothe your cough, like humidifiers, fluids, and warm tea, and save medicine for emergencies after speaking with your doctor. Remember, online advice isn't a replacement for a healthcare provider's guidance.",
